<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila Development Bank samurai planned for July.</title>
<headline>Manila Development Bank samurai planned for July.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Development Bank of the Philippines will hold a roadshow for its planned six-year samurai bond on July 20-25, Finance Secretary Roberto de Ocampo said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The bond will be worth the equivalent of $160 million and be used for housing loans, de Ocampo told reorters.</p>
<p>He expected it to carry a 3-4 percent interest rate.</p>
<p>Daiwa Securities is lead manager.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841 8914</p>
</text>
